From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:06:42 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] compositor: Draw server-side decorations for Wayland
 toplevels

Add MetaWindowDecoration, a child of the Wayland window actor that draws
the titlebar and border of a toplevel that negotiated server-side
decorations with xdg-decoration. It sits below the client's surfaces and
covers the frame rect, plus an invisible resize margin while the window
is floating; it is dropped for fullscreen windows.

The look follows the default GNOME titlebar: a light headerbar with the
window title in the titlebar-font, centered and ellipsized, round
symbolic buttons in the button-layout order (menu, minimize, maximize or
restore, close, as far as the window supports them), a backdrop style
for unfocused windows and a translucent 1 px border. libmutter has no
cairo without Xwayland, so the button images are rasterized with 4x4
supersampling into Cogl textures, at the actor's resource scale.

meta_display_handle_event() hands pointer events on a decoration to
meta_window_decoration_handle_event() after the usual click-to-focus
and raise. Buttons highlight on hover and press, and act on release
over the same button. A titlebar press starts a move grab; the double,
middle and right click titlebar actions are honoured. The edges and
corners start resize grabs and set resize cursors. Motion is still
passed on, so the client gets its leave event.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
